          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            A
            %em stratified simplicial set
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+set"} simplicial set
            equipped with information about which of its
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplex"} simplices
            are to be regarded as being
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/thin+element"} thin
            in that they are like identities or at least like equivalences in a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+category+theory"} higher category
          %p
            The theory of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+weak+%E2%88%9E-categories"} simplicial weak ∞-categories
            is based on stratified simplicial sets.
          %h2#definition Definition
          %p
            A
            %strong stratification
            of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+set"} simplicial set
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mo :
                  %msup
                    %mi Δ
                    %mi op
                  %mo →
                  %mi Set
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X : \Delta^{op} \to Set
            is a subset
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi t
                  %mi X
                  %mo ⊂
                  %msub
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∐
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %msub
                    %mi X
                    %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} t X \subset \coprod_{[n]} X_n
            of its set of simplices (not in general a simplicial subset!) such that
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                no 0-simplex of
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                is in
                = succeed ";" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi t
                        %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} t X
            %li
              %p
                every degenerate simplex in
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                is in
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi t
                        %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} t X
          %p
            A
            %strong stratified simplicial set
            is a pair
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi t
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (X, t X)
            consisting of a simplicial set
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            and a stratification
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi t
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} t X
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
          %p
            The elements of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi t
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} t X
            are called the
            %strong thin
            simplices of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
          %p
            For
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi t
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (X, t X)
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Y
                  %mo ,
                  %mi t
                  %mi Y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (Y, t Y)
            stratified simplicial sets, a morphism
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo :
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f : X \to Y
            of simplicial sets is set to be a
            %strong stratified map
            if it respects thin cells in that
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi t
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ⊂
                  %mi t
                  %mi Y
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  f(t X ) \subset t Y
                  \\,.
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            of stratified simplicial sets and stratified maps between them is usually denoted
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Strat
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Strat
          %p
            This category is a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quasitopos"} quasitopos
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cartesian+closed+category"} cartesian closed
          %h2#examples Examples
          %ul
            %li
              %p Every simplicial set gives rise to a stratified simplicial set
              %ul
                %li
                  %p
                    using the
                    = succeed ":" do
                      %strong maximal stratification
                %li
                  %p
                    using the
                    = succeed ":" do
                      %strong minimal stratification
              %p
                These two stratifications give
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+adjoint"} left
                and
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/right+adjoints"} right adjoints
                to the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/forgetful+functor"} forgetful functor
                from stratified simplicial sets to simplicial sets.
            %li
              %p
                The
                %strong standard thin
                = succeed "-" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
                %strong simplex
                is obtained from
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Δ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta[n]
                by making its only non-degenerate
                = succeed "-simplex" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            %li
              %p
                The
                = succeed "th" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi k
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
                %strong standard admissible
                = succeed "-" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
                %strong simplex
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msubsup
                          %mi Δ
                          %mi k
                          %mi a
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %mi n
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta^a_k[n]
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo ≥
                        %mn 2
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \geq 2
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mn 0
                        %mo &lt;
                        %mi k
                        %mo &lt;
                        %mi n
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0 \lt k \lt n
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Δ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta[n]
                by making all simplices
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi α
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mi m
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mo →
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha \colon [m] \to [n]
                with
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi k
                      %mo −
                      %mn 1
                      %mo ,
                      %mi k
                      %mo ,
                      %mi k
                      %mo +
                      %mn 1
                      %mo ∈
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k-1,k,k+1 \in
                im
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi α
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\alpha)
                thin.
            %li
              %p
                The
                %strong standard admissible
                = succeed "-" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi n
                        %mo −
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (n-1)
                %strong dimensional
                = succeed "-" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi k
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
                %strong horn
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msubsup
                          %mi Λ
                          %mi k
                          %mi a
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %mi n
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Lambda^a_k[n]
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo ≥
                        %mn 2
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \geq 2
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mn 0
                        %mo &lt;
                        %mi k
                        %mo &lt;
                        %mi n
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0 \lt k \lt n
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msubsup
                          %mi Δ
                          %mi k
                          %mi a
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %mi n
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta^a_k[n]
            %li
              %p
                A
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complicial+set"} complicial set
                is a stratified simplicial set satisfying certain extra conditions. Complicial sets are precisely those simplicial sets which arise (up to isomorphism) as the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/oriental"} ∞-nerve
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi N
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi C
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N(C)
                of a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strict+%E2%88%9E-category"} strict ∞-category
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi C
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi C
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            %li
              %p
                A
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+set"} simplicial set
                is a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kan+complex"} Kan complex
                precisely if its maximal stratification makes it a
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weak+complicial+set"} weak complicial set
          %h2#the_category_of_stratified_simplicial_sets The category of stratified simplicial sets
          %p
            There are several
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+products"} tensor products
            on the category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Strat
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Strat
            of stratified simplicial sets that make it a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+category"} monoidal category
          %h3#strat_with_the_veritygray_tensor_product Strat with the Verity-Gray tensor product
          %p
            Consider the monoidal category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Strat
                  %mo ,
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (Strat, \otimes)
            where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ⊗
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \otimes
            is the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Verity-Gray+tensor+product"} Verity-Gray tensor product
          %p
            (Notice that this is not
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/closed+monoidal+category"} closed
          %p
            Using the canonical stratification of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/oriental"} ∞-nerves
            on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strict+%E2%88%9E-categories"} strict ∞-categories
            as
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complicial+sets"} complicial sets
            = succeed "-nerve" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ω
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \omega
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi N
                  %mo :
                  %mi Str
                  %mi ω
                  %mi Cat
                  %mo →
                  %mi Strat
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  N : Str \omega Cat \to Strat
                  \\,.
          .un_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              The functor
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi N
                    %mo :
                    %mi Str
                    %mi ω
                    %mi Cat
                    %mo →
                    %mi Strat
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N : Str \omega Cat \to Strat
              has a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+adjoint"} left adjoint
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                    %mo :
                    %mi Strat
                    %mo →
                    %mi Str
                    %mi ω
                    %mi Cat
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F : Strat \to Str \omega Cat
              which is a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strong+monoidal+functor"} strong monoidal functor
          %p
            Or so it is claimed on
            %a{:href => "http://www.mat.uc.pt/~categ/ct2007/slides/verity.pdf#page=60"} slide 60
            of
            %a{:href => "http://www.mat.uc.pt/~categ/ct2007/slides/verity.pdf"} Ver07
          %h2#references References
          %p A useful quick introduction is the beginning of these slides:
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dominic+Verity"}> Dominic Verity
              ,
              %em Weak Complicial sets and internal quasi-categories
              (
              %a{:href => "http://www.mat.uc.pt/~categ/ct2007/slides/verity.pdf"}> pdf slides
              )
